              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "counseljul50"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used regular canned salmon, added about 1 t. liquid smoke, and saved the money of purchasing smoked salmon, and got more comments on it than when I used real smoked salmon."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marytime"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't' have the heavy cream or green onions so I substituted 2 TBSP cream cheese, 1 TBSP of milk, and used 1/2 tsp onion powder. It didn't have the nice green of the onions so I added a Tsp of parsley too. Tastes even better the next day.",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-14T16:52:56.120Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kenny Dombrosky"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made the salmon spread for one of our appetizers on Xmas day. Instead of serving it as a dip, I spread it on flour tortillas, and rolled them, refrigerated them overnight, and sliced them, and served them as pinwheels. They were a big hit.",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-27T20:58:02.197Z"
          },
          {
